Z||000000||hugh||03-23-2001||07:54 PM||||I'm in the process of doing the suspension on my 88.I have a bent rear sway bar.Since I need to replace it,what would be the best way to go.Stock or would it be better to use a bigger one(if they are even available)?Does anyone have one to sell? I should mention I have Ryane struts with coilovers in the rear and Ryanes tubular upper and lower control arms with coilovers in the front.I got alignment specs.off the forum before,but I've been thinking-my car weighs 3400 lbs.  1200 in the front and 2200 in the rear with a tank of gas and me in it.What would be the best specs for this particular car?Any other ideas you can offer will be greatly appreciated. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hugh_sig.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by hugh (edited 03-23-2001).]||||reg||1
