Z||000003||hugh||03-25-2001||07:54 AM||||Can anyone help with the alignment specs?||||reg||1
Z||000004||daved||03-25-2001||09:05 AM||||There is a lot of information here if you use the "search" function, but these specs I have gleaned from previous posts on the subject (thanks Forum):<BR>Below are the specs for all.<BR>FRONT<BR>Caster min 3.0* max 7.0*<BR>Camber Min -0.3* max 1.3*<BR>Toe min .05* max 0.25*<BR>Total Toe min 0.15* max 0.50*<BR>SAI should be set to 7.5* <BR>REAR<BR>Camber min -1.5* max -0.5*<BR>Toe min -0.1* max 0.1*<BR>Total Toe min -0.2* max 0.2*<BR>Thrust angle less than -1.0*<P>Another member posted "After 12 years of playing around with alignment #'s this is what I currently use: <BR>Front: 4.5 to 5 deg. pos. caster, .5 to 1 deg. neg. camber, usually a little bit of toe-in (1/16"). <BR>Rear: 1.5 to 2 deg. neg. camber, ALWAYS a little bit of toe-in."<BR>Hope that helps, Dave <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||03-25-2001||02:41 PM||||Don't forget that the '88's use different alignment specs than previous years.  I don't know them offhand, but am looking...||||reg||1
